/**
 * Washington Real Estate Fundamentals (60 clock hours) — module question bank.
 *
 * ONE OF THE TWO COURSES RCW 18.85.101(1)(c) NAMES. The statute requires "90 hours of instruction in real
 * estate," and provides that instruction "must include courses as prescribed by the director including
 * FUNDAMENTALS, WHICH SHALL INCLUDE THREE HOURS OF INSTRUCTION ON FAIR HOUSING AND CONSUMER PROTECTION
 * ISSUES, and PRACTICES." It names both courses and ALLOCATES HOURS TO NEITHER.
 *
 * WASHINGTON LICENSES A BROKER, NOT A SALESPERSON. RCW 18.86.010(3): "'Broker' means broker, managing
 * broker, and designated broker, collectively." Every item uses Washington's own words. No item may refer
 * to a Washington "salesperson."
 *
 * THE THREE-HOUR FAIR HOUSING AND CONSUMER PROTECTION BLOCK IS MODULE-09, DELIVERED AT EXACTLY 3.0 HOURS
 * so a reviewer can audit it in one place. The engine asserts it, and a test asserts the engine.
 *
 * THE EXAMINATION THIS COURSE MUST CARRY IS SET BY RULE AND IT SCALES. WAC 308-124H-820(8): "Courses of 30
 * clock hours or more ... must include a comprehensive examination(s) and answer key(s) of no fewer than
 * THREE QUESTIONS PER CLOCK HOUR with a MINIMUM OF 90 QUESTIONS, and a requirement of passing course grade
 * of AT LEAST 70 PERCENT." At 60 clock hours that is A MINIMUM OF 180 ITEMS. The 70 percent is the
 * DIRECTOR'S figure. The items in this bank are NOT that examination — they gate progression through a
 * module and are visible to the student by design, and the 80 percent engagement threshold is a StateCourse
 * standard.
 *
 * A WASHINGTON CLOCK HOUR IS 50 MINUTES OF ACTUAL INSTRUCTION — WAC 308-124H-820(4). So this course is
 * 3,000 minutes of instruction.
 *
 * THE DEPARTMENT PRESCRIBES THE CURRICULUM AND THIS PROJECT DOES NOT HAVE IT. WAC 308-124H-810: an approved
 * school "must utilize the most recent course curriculum prescribed by the department." Everything here is
 * authored from RCW 18.85.101, RCW 18.86 and WAC 308-124H, read on 2026-08-20. Conforming to the
 * Department's curriculum is a submission gate.
 *
 * Each module carries one applied item, five engagement items and five remediation items. The correct answer
 * is authored at index 0 and permuted deterministically per item id at delivery, so a recorded selection
 * keeps its meaning permanently. The public delivery path strips correctChoice and rationale, and a test
 * proves it.
 *
 * WHAT WAS NOT READ, AND WHICH THEREFORE APPEARS IN NO ITEM: the Department's prescribed curriculum;
 * WAC 308-124A-800 and -802; the remainder of RCW 18.85 including RCW 18.85.011 and 18.85.361; WAC 308-124
 * and its trust account, advertising and retention rules; the RCW 18.86.120 pamphlet text; RCW 64.06 and the
 * seller disclosure statement; RCW 59.18; RCW 49.60 and the federal Fair Housing Act; RCW 82.45 and every
 * local excise tax ordinance; RCW 61.24; Washington's recording, intestacy, community property, condominium
 * and lien statutes; ARELLO's standards; USPAP; and TILA, RESPA, TRID and ECOA. NO ITEM asks a student to
 * recall a figure, deadline or provision from any of them. Every rate in every item is supplied inside the
 * item as a given.
 *
 * Course version 1.0 submission draft — NOT APPROVED. No Washington clock hours are available.
 */

